From: Leszek Swirski <leszeks@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:56:00 +0100
Subject: [compiler] Ignore stale kReceiver call feedback on non-apply calls

CallIC only records a receiver with CallFeedbackContent::kReceiver when
initializing monomorphic feedback for Function.prototype.apply with a
callable receiver. Subsequent calls at the same site can transition the
slot to a FeedbackCell or megamorphic, or match the recorded function in
a direct call, without clearing the kReceiver bit.

Normalize CallFeedbackContent to kTarget in
JSHeapBroker::ReadFeedbackForCall when the feedback target is not
callable, and skip Function.prototype.apply speculation in
MaglevGraphBuilder::BuildCallWithFeedback when the call target is
already a known constant other than apply. Drive-by, add DCHECKs that
kReceiver feedback only ever accompanies a callable target.

